 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A Russian warship sank in Libya, far from Ukraine. How did drones get there?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "The corvette Merkury was docked in Benghazi on Sunday when explosions hit it. Libya's eastern authorities say it was refuelling and suspect a drone attack. Defense News says it is mostly underwater. A Russian cargo ship was hit too."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "President Zelensky said on Monday Ukraine did it, with seven home-made sea drones. That is about seventeen hundred kilometres from the front line, SBS reports. How the drones got there is unclear. Albania denies they were launched from its soil."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Russia's ambassador to Libya told RT that Kyiv is trying to widen the war at sea. The Kremlin says it has taken note. Eastern Libya's prime minister wants a UN probe into whether the boats came from western Libya. The UN mission urges restraint."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Ukraine hit another Russian ship abroad before New Year? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
